Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["InfraMessageFunction", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"402c773e-74ac-472e-89f3-cc42ddfd1323"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraMessageFunction"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraMessageFunction", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["b", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "82627a11-46ea-48f4-8d54-daafccb54fbd"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is the message relation from the observer ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " to the observer ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ": each tick of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " goes to the ticks of ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " that its light rays reach. Its members are the message functions, the \
single-valued selections of the relation that preserve the order of the \
ticks.",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"1f323bef-6ff0-4313-91d0-4c698ec8a412"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: for observers ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ", chains given as vertex lists in causal order, the message relation sends \
a tick ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") = ",
 StyleBox["E", "TI"],
 "\:207a(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") \:2229 ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ", the ticks of ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " on the future light cone of ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ". A message function is a map ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 " from the ticks ",
 StyleBox["a'", "TI"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " with a message to ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " such that ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") \[Element] ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") for every ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " in ",
 StyleBox["a'", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 " does not reverse the order: if ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " comes before ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 " on ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ", then ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") does not come after ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 ") on ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c897b8a5-d332-461d-b869-e9f5f4d5fcac"],

Cell["\<\
In Minkowski space a light signal from an event of one particle reaches the \
other particle at exactly one event, and the map preserves the order of the \
clocks. On a graph a light cone can meet an observer in several ticks, or in \
none: the relation is set-valued and partial, and the message functions are \
its consistent single-valued choices. There can be many, or exactly one, as \
on the diamond lattice between two parallel null lines.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4b7df6f6-d5ff-445d-ac8a-c76bb75cf98a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The head holds its two observers and computes nothing. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1d534c86-130a-4415-8b32-5139ee817367"],
 " reads it on a graph:"
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b77c7fd6-881d-4e7a-908b-a12e8cbc779f"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "3cfd6781-0443-4acd-a2c9-fd770214395d"], Cell["Property", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"9bdf4968-15c8-46bd-823e-cc3bc9e97aa9"],
